1
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,833
Dear May Deer,

2
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,667
With a lovely family,

3
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:15,250
Dreaming of growing up each day.

4
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,167
Shy Chuan-Chuan Pangolin,

5
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,667
Quiet, with not a word to say,

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:22,333
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

7
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:23,917
Don’t be shy!

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,833
Sing out loud!

9
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:29,419
Let your imagination shine!

10
00:00:29,429 --> 00:00:31,167
Good friends in the forest,

11
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:33,083
Growing and playing together,

12
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:37,500
Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan!

13
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:40,082
What to Do When You Can’t Sleep

14
00:00:40,667 --> 00:00:45,167
This is the story of May Deer, a sika deer who lives in a forest town.

15
00:00:46,083 --> 00:00:49,750
Tonight, May Deer and Little Deer are getting ready for bed.

16
00:00:51,167 --> 00:00:54,000
That milk was delicious. My tummy feels all warm now.

17
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,667
May, time to brush your teeth and go to bed!

18
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,500
Brush, brush, brush your teeth!

19
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,417
Say bye-bye to those cavity bugs!

20
00:01:03,167 --> 00:01:05,917
May, Little Deer, story time!

21
00:01:06,917 --> 00:01:09,083
Their bedtime story every night

22
00:01:09,083 --> 00:01:11,417
is the part of the day May and Little Deer look forward to most.

23
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:14,667
But tonight, Little Deer doesn’t seem interested in a story.

24
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:16,833
He seems to be looking for something.

25
00:01:16,833 --> 00:01:20,083
And they all lived happily ever after.

26
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:23,917
The story’s over, little ones.

27
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:26,000
Good night, Mom.

28
00:01:33,167 --> 00:01:36,667
But May Deer just couldn’t fall asleep.

29
00:01:43,167 --> 00:01:44,750
Little Deer, what’s wrong?

30
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,917
Towel!

31
00:01:49,167 --> 00:01:51,167
Can’t you sleep either?

32
00:01:52,667 --> 00:01:55,417
I know! I’ll sing you a lullaby.

33
00:01:56,250 --> 00:02:04,750
Sleep, my little one. I love you.

34
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:10,500
Towel!

35
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:13,167
I know you’re looking for your little towel,

36
00:02:13,417 --> 00:02:15,167
but I don’t know where it is either.

37
00:02:15,167 --> 00:02:18,083
All right, then. I’ll tell you another bedtime story.

38
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,417
Little Deer

39
00:02:19,417 --> 00:02:21,750
Have you heard the story of the Ten Suns?

40
00:02:22,083 --> 00:02:23,917
Once upon a time,

41
00:02:23,917 --> 00:02:27,167
there was a giant dinosaur in the sky who loved to eat.

42
00:02:27,167 --> 00:02:28,667
He could eat absolutely anything!

43
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,750
There were ten suns in the sky.

44
00:02:30,833 --> 00:02:32,917
Every one of them was mischievous.

45
00:02:32,917 --> 00:02:34,750
They were making everyone burn up!

46
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:36,750
It’s so hot!

47
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:39,750
Mr. Dinosaur, can you help us?

48
00:02:39,917 --> 00:02:42,750
To help everyone, Mr. Dinosaur

49
00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:45,500
ate one sun, then two, then three…

50
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,417
But when he was about to eat the tenth sun…

51
00:02:48,417 --> 00:02:49,250
No, no!

52
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:50,417
If you eat them all,

53
00:02:50,417 --> 00:02:53,000
there won’t be any sun left for us!

54
00:02:53,833 --> 00:02:57,333
So Mr. Dinosaur let out a huge burp.

55
00:02:57,583 --> 00:03:00,250
Then he lay down on Earth and fell asleep.

56
00:03:00,917 --> 00:03:02,750
Ta-da! The story is over!

57
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:03,917
Wasn’t that a good story?

58
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,583
Little Deer, did you like the story?

59
00:03:09,917 --> 00:03:13,500
Looks like you still can’t sleep. What should I do?

60
00:03:13,667 --> 00:03:14,750
I’ve got it!

61
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:16,750
Let’s count sheep.

62
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:18,750
Sheepies!

63
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:21,417
Close your eyes and lie down slowly.

64
00:03:21,917 --> 00:03:22,917
Oh!

65
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,000
I’m going to start counting.

66
00:03:27,333 --> 00:03:28,917
No peeking!

67
00:03:29,917 --> 00:03:31,917
What to Do When You Can’t Sleep

68
00:03:31,917 --> 00:03:34,000
The little sheep are here to say good night.

69
00:03:34,750 --> 00:03:37,250
One little sheep is coming in!

70
00:03:40,917 --> 00:03:42,583
They’re all here to sleep with us.

71
00:03:43,083 --> 00:03:46,917
Two sheep, three sheep, four sheep…

72
00:03:47,417 --> 00:03:52,083
As May counted, more and more sheep came in, one by one.

73
00:03:52,083 --> 00:03:56,500
Eight sheep, nine sheep, ten sheep!

74
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:59,417
They’re all around our room.

75
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:01,417
All the sheep are here!

76
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:03,667
Little Deer, open your eyes!

77
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:16,000
The whole flock is here to sleep with you.

78
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:18,250
Wow, what a cute hat!

79
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,000
They all snore, too!

80
00:04:23,667 --> 00:04:26,000
Little Deer, are you sleepy now?

81
00:04:31,167 --> 00:04:31,417
Oh, dear.

82
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:33,833
It’s a little lamb!

83
00:04:35,833 --> 00:04:37,917
Can you help us?

84
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,750
Towel!

85
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:46,000
Little Deer found his little towel!

86
00:04:46,583 --> 00:04:48,750
Hooray! You found your little towel!

87
00:04:59,917 --> 00:05:01,167
Hehehe!

88
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:02,750
You’ve been squished flat!

89
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:03,750
Hehehe!

90
00:05:03,750 --> 00:05:04,667
Good night! Bye-bye!

91
00:05:06,083 --> 00:05:09,500
One sheep, two sheep…

92
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:13,750
Three sheep, four sheep…

93
00:05:13,750 --> 00:05:17,083
Five sheep, six sheep…

94
00:05:17,083 --> 00:05:20,417
Seven sheep, eight sheep…

95
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:23,833
Good night, everyone.

96
00:05:28,667 --> 00:05:31,833
At last, May Deer and Little Deer fell asleep.

97
00:05:31,833 --> 00:05:34,417
Together, they drifted off into beautiful dreams.
